      "ok": true,
      "detail": "pe = 0..20 at N = 40 rows: max over frames 2.159802376118285961604.  The best NON-EMPTY move at any optimum gains -0.000759437, so the certificate does not rest on rounding (the gains are evaluated at mp.dps = 25).  The deepest support is 27 rows, well inside N.  By Murota's L-natural optimality theorem each is the exact integer maximum for its (pe, N); the BMAX = 10 enumeration recorded 2.159802376118285961604"
    },
    {
      "name": "M7 the tail lemma holds at every certified frame",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "per-row bound eps(b_N + 1) + cbar_N <= 0.0026554678 against (ln q0)/2 = 0.05217036 at N = 40, pe = 0..20.  So any move touching a row >= N gains strictly less than the same move without those rows, which M5 already showed is <= 0: the N-row maximum is the maximum over EVERY block length"
    },
    {
      "name": "M7b longer blocks agree: no move improves the padded optimum at T = N + 4, N + 12",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "best +-chi_S gain at pe in (0, 3, 20), T in (N + 4, N + 12): 1.65436e-24"
    },
    {
      "name": "M8 G_{pe+1}(0, u) = G_pe(u)",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "40 random points, pe 0..12: max difference 6.204e-25.  Rows j >= 1 of frame pe + 1 sit one position above rows j - 1 of frame pe with the same gaps and wall weights, and the bottom row's pair term eps(b) - eps(b + x) plus the one-body sum over b + 1..b + x is exactly the one-body sum over b..b + x - 1"
    },
    {
      "name": "M9 eps(1) < ln q0 * (PEMAX + 1)",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "eps(1) = 1.669473278 < ln q0 * 21 = 2.191155127.  In frame pe + 1 >= 21, raising the bottom row by x >= 1 gains at most x eps(1) in its one-body term, pays ln q0 (pe + 1) x on the wall, and only loses on its pairs (they close).  So zeroing it never lowers G, and with M8 sup(frame pe + 1) = sup(frame pe) for every pe >= 20: the frames beyond PEMAX add nothing"
    },
    {
      "name": "M6 the G1-free cut is enumerable for every frame and block length",
